AGENTS.md:19:Frontend data flow has a few owning modules, each documented under "Remote Forms" and "TanStack Query with the Phoenix API" in `docs/agents/critical-patterns.md`: one Valibot schema per form in `lib/schemas/` (built from `fields.ts`; output is the generated request body; dates stay `YYYY-MM-DD` strings), `apiProblem` in `lib/api-error.ts` for every Phoenix error (`detail`/`code`/`fields`), `inventoryCommand` for quartermaster remote forms (the Items page sends every Item command through one, with its outcome in `item-workbench.svelte.ts`, and property values through `lib/inventory/property-values.ts`), `lib/inventory/member-loans.svelte.ts` for member Loan transitions, and `createCursorTableUrl` for URL-backed cursor tables. Every Dublin date or time — Dublin today, a civil `YYYY-MM-DD` ↔ date-picker `CalendarDate`, an instant on the Dublin clock, a formatted civil date — comes from `lib/club-calendar.ts` (ALE-418); do not bridge with `parseDate`/dayjs or build an `Intl.DateTimeFormat` in a context (the `anti-slop/no-dublin-time-zone-literal` rule catches only the zone literal). Runes controllers (`*.svelte.ts`) are tested as `*.svelte.browser.test.ts` because the unit project runs Svelte's server build; see "SvelteKit (current)" in `docs/agents/notes.md`.
docs/agents/where-to-look.md:61:| Change the quartermaster Items page | `apps/web/src/routes/dashboard/inventory/items/[[itemId]]/item-workbench.svelte.ts` (runes controller) + `data.remote.ts` (every Item command) + `apps/web/src/lib/schemas/inventoryItem.ts` + `apps/web/src/lib/inventory/property-values.ts` + `item-workbench.svelte.browser.test.ts` | ALE-416. The page only renders and binds. The controller owns the URL-backed list request (`createCursorTableUrl`, filters `archived`/`availability`, page size 25), routed selection (`[[itemId]]`, `new`, the `?slug=` deep link), the drafts and their dirty state, and each command's outcome: a management form flashes its button and adopts the item Phoenix answered with; archive and restore toast; delete returns to the list. Item routes carry the list's query string so "All items" returns to the same search. Every Item command (create, update, move, change category, start/end maintenance, archive, restore, delete) is a remote form through `inventoryCommand`, spread as `form.preflight(schema).enhance(workbench.enhance.<command>)`; do not add a TanStack mutation for one. Property values are one draft map (`property-values.ts`: conversion from an item, the JSON hidden field, `sameDraft`, Yes/No and decimal display, shared with the member equipment view). The generated `vInventoryOperatorItemValues` is an empty `v.object({})` that strips every value, so decode a draft with `decodePropertyDraft`, never with it. |
docs/agents/critical-patterns.md:230:- URL-backed cursor tables (Waitlist, members, invitations) use `createCursorTableUrl` (`#lib/cursor-table-url.svelte.js`): it owns key prefixing, sort/page-size fallback, the TanStack sorting/pagination adapter, and history (replace for search/filters/sort/page size, push for cursor paging). Search is a debounced draft; a pending draft is written together with any other replace, so a reset is just `setSearch("")` then `setFilter(key, null)`; clear several filters with one `setFilters({...})`, since a second separate replace is built from a URL that may not yet show the first. `defaultPageSize` sets a table's page size when the URL names none (the Items page uses 25).
docs/agents/tech-stack.md:13:- **Workflow state machines**: XState v5 (`xstate`, `@xstate/svelte`). Two shapes only: pure `initialTransition`/`transition` on the server (Invitation Acceptance, ADR 0024), and per-component `useMachine` actors in the browser (Invitation Acceptance payment, workshop express checkout, Training Announcement save). Never a module-scope actor. Adopt a browser machine only for a temporal protocol with mutually exclusive phases, stage-aware retry/cancel, and coordinated async work — not to wrap TanStack Query or independent form values.
docs/agents/where-to-look.md:103:| Change how the SvelteKit frontend reacts to an Invitation Acceptance state (initial page, resume, payment, verification, Discord restart, cookies) | `apps/web/src/lib/server/invitation-acceptance/` (`index.ts` public; `decision.ts` pure XState decision machine, `workflow.ts` operations, `apply.ts` effects → data/redirect, `ports.ts`, `api-client-adapter.ts`, `cookie-store.ts`, `testing.ts` in-memory adapters) + `apps/web/src/lib/invitation-acceptance/` (`vocabulary.ts` statuses + valibot schema, `presentation.ts`, `payment-machine.ts` browser UI machine, `paths.ts`) + `apps/web/src/routes/(public)/members/signup/[invitationId]/` (thin route/remote adapters, `payment-form.svelte` host, `payment-submit.svelte` per-state UI) | GH-509 / ADR 0024. **Phoenix is the only authority**; this module owns the frontend's interpretation of the safe-view `state` (both Phoenix spellings normalise onto one vocabulary; an unknown status is rejected, never rendered as step 1), the valid route outcomes (`SHOW`, `REDIRECT_TO_SUCCESS`, `RESTART_VERIFICATION`, `UNAVAILABLE`, `REJECTED`), and the cookie effects each outcome requests (`clearAcceptanceProof`, `storeProof`, `establishSignInHandoff`). Every route and remote command converges on `decideInvitationRoute` through one `workflow.ts` operation and then `applyInvitationRouteOutcome` — do not read `response.data.state` or touch `_dhc_onboarding_acceptance` in a route. The decision runs through XState's pure `initialTransition`/`transition`; **never create an actor at module scope** (server modules are shared across requests). The payment step's browser work is `paymentMachine` (`deciding → initializing → ready → preparing → submitting`, plus `failed`/`expired`/`unavailable`), instantiated per component with `useMachine` and stopped with it; Stripe objects and the remote form stay in `payment-form.svelte` as provided actors/actions, and the machine has no `accepted` state because success redirects after Phoenix reconciles. Both presentation records are exhaustive `satisfies Record<…>`; adding a status or state without deciding its UI is a type error. Tests: `decision.test.ts`, `workflow.test.ts`, `apply.test.ts`, `api-client-adapter.test.ts`, `vocabulary.test.ts`, `payment-machine.test.ts` (unit) and `payment-submit.browser.test.ts` (browser). The real Phoenix + Stripe seam is `e2e/protected-invitation-acceptance.spec.ts`. |
docs/agents/where-to-look.md:106:| Run structural lint | `mise run ast-lint` | ast-grep rules from `.ast-grep/rules/` (config: `sgconfig.yml`). Enforces the `created_at` timestamp convention on Ecto migrations, no bare `fetch` in web source, and no XState actor (`createActor`/`useMachine`/`useActor`) in SvelteKit server code (`no-xstate-actor-in-server-code`, ADR 0024). Validate rule fixtures with `mise run ast-test`. The LSP is wired in `opencode.json` for live diagnostics. |

